Usage: fold [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Wrap input lines to fit specified width.

Write each FILE to standard output, wrapping input lines to fit in width columns.
With no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.

Note: This implementation supports basic folding.
Some locale-specific character-width details remain approximate on Windows.

OPTIONS:
  -b, --bytes       count bytes rather than columns
  -c, --characters  count characters rather than columns
  -s, --spaces      break at spaces
  -w, --width ARG   use WIDTH columns instead of 80
      --help        display this help and exit
  -V, --version     output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
